NNAAMMEE
     ccoolloorr..44tthh — FreeBSD color-detection boot module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The file that goes by the name of ccoolloorr..44tthh is a set of commands designed
     to simplify color logic.  The commands of ccoolloorr..44tthh by themselves are not
     enough for most uses.  Please refer to the examples below for the most
     common situations, and to loader(8) for additional commands.

     Before using any of the commands provided in ccoolloorr..44tthh, it must be in‐
     cluded through the command:

           include color.4th

     This line is present in _/_b_o_o_t_/_l_o_a_d_e_r_._4_t_h file, so it is not needed (and
     should not be re-issued) in a normal setup.

     The commands provided by it are:

           llooaaddeerr__ccoolloorr??          Returns FALSE if the llooaaddeerr__ccoolloorr environ‐
                                  ment variable is set to “NO” (case-insensi‐
                                  tive) or “0”.  Otherwise returns TRUE
                                  (unless booting serial).

     The environment variables that effect its behavior are:

           _l_o_a_d_e_r___c_o_l_o_r
                     If set to “NO” (case-insensitive) or “0”, causes
                     llooaaddeerr__ccoolloorr?? to return FALSE, indicating to many modules
                     that color should not be used.

